WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.360
Mr. Handa's Group Blind Date?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.370
I'm terribly sorry.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.200
What happened?

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.790
When I asked for my usual, 
she brought me pot stickers.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.370
Have I ever ordered pot stickers here?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.760
Haven't you?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.260
No.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.720
We don't have pot stickers on the menu.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.140
You're right.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.140
You went through the 
trouble of making them?

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.600
Yes.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.530
Well done, Miss Sasako!

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.550
Is this really where 
you compliment her?

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.990
It was delicious.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.260
Really?

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.270
Is this really where you get happy?

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.760
Oh, whatever. Could I get my usual?

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.500
Sure.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:28.710
What is this?

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.140
The Pot Sticker Lunch.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:33.180
Have I ever ordered this?

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.220
Never.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.840
Are you playing around?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.570
Yup.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.300
I'm so tired.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.910
You've been working hard.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.780
Could I get my usual?

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.340
Your usual, huh?

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.130
One Pot Sticker Lunch, Miss Sasako.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:54.730
One large serving of bamboo and 
an iced coffee coming right up.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.780
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.120
Hey, listen to this.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.490
Today...

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.220
Really? It's already time?

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.930
I'm still tired.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.900
I'm going back to sleep.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.560
Wait a minute.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.640
You want to talk about how 
you went back to sleep?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.340
I wasn't sure where 
to start my story.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.170
Could you try again when 
you have a better idea?

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:36.700
I don't really have time.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.650
Oh, okay.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.700
Good morning, Kirino.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.160
Good morning, Panda.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.310
It's not exactly morning.
 You're late.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.040
Mr. Handa's lunch.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.280
I think I'll open it.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.020
Don't do that, Panda.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.120
Just a peek.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.600
No!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.480
Don't do it.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.990
Just a peek.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.330
What a very brown lunch.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.500
It's like a granny's lunch.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.250
Wait a minute.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.090
You wanted to talk about his lunch?

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.420
Jeez. I'm still in the 
middle of my story.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.220
Come on. I don't have all day.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.380
You're not busy, though.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.220
You're always here.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:58.490
What do you do all day, Mr. Penguin?

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.720
J-Just hurry up and get to the point.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.240
Okay.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.130
Panda,

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:11.240
there'll be a group of elementary schoolers

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.740
coming in this afternoon, so let's

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.700
make sure to give them extra service.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:15.970
Okay!

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.330
I'll make sure to roll 
around more than usual.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:27.090
Hey, Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.480
Yes?

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:32.190
I saw Mr. Handa's lunch today.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:38.310
It was really brown, and looked 
like a granny's lunch.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.270
But it was really good.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.650
You ate it?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:43.940
Yup!

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:46.860
You ate it...

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:53.040
Yup. The lunch was really 
good, but how do I put it...

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.870
It really seemed like a lunch 
prepared by a guy for a guy...

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:01.820
Well, it was a lunch that Mr. 
Handa put together for himself.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:08.140
But it seemed like a lunch that 
a granny made for a granny.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.340
In a word, it was

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.300
unappealing.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:16.050
It seemed like a really 
unappealing lunch.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:20.810
I wish I had seen this unappealing lunch.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.110
I can hear you.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.570
We said it so you would hear.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.900
Could you show me

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:29.780
this unappealing lunch 
next time, Mr. Handa?

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.380
Hey, that's quite rude.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.160
Then are you popular?

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:39.080
Have you talked to a girl recently?

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.040
What are you talking 
about all of a sudden?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.500
I'm asking you if you've 
talked to a girl recently.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.220
Huh? U-Um... Oh!

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.590
Other than your mom.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.990
U-Um...

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.140
Oh!

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.300
Other than animals.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.310
Um, um...

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.770
You see?

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:06.780
How weird.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:13.160
Since you're so unappealing, 
I asked Kirino for you.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.790
Huh? Asked him what?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:19.490
Mr. Handa! It's done!

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:20.810
What?

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.790
The group blind date!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.540
Panda said you wanted to do it.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:29.210
I never said that. I'm not going.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.880
What? Hold on a minute.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.920
I set this up for you, Mr. Handa.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.390
The girls are all offices ladies.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.390
But I'm busy.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.390
You have something going on?

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.310
I have to go home and 
clean my bathroom.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.280
That wouldn't fall under busy.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.740
You're going, right, Mr. Handa?

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:58.360
Please look after Mr. Handa, Kirino.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.700
Could you not make the 
decisions for me?

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.080
Let's go, Mr. Handa.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.130
Mr. Handa!

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.590
I-I won't say yes just because you're cute.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.970
Kirino set this up for you 
because Panda asked him to,

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.260
even though he's never been to one.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:20.200
I've been to a few...

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.190
Mr. Handa, you should totally go.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.650
Don't worry about it, you two.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:29.920
All right, I understand.

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:33.610
If you really don't want to go 
that much, I'll cancel.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.010
A-All right, I'll go!

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.120
Really?!

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:39.440
Thank goodness.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.620
The guys' side will be us and my friend,

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.420
so it'll be 3 and 3.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.790
It'll be at 7PM.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.400
Okay.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:52.370
You can't show the 
office ladies your lunch.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:53.760
I-I won't.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.420
Thanks for your hard work today.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.690
Good luck at your group 
blind date tonight!

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.640
Shhhhh! You're too loud!

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.100
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.260
All right, see you tomorrow.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.020
Okay.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.360
This will change 
Mr. Handa's lunch for sure.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.490
Wait, what? Are you serious?

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.080
All right, got it.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:22.910
This isn't good.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:24.960
What happened?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.190
It's about tonight's group blind date,

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:30.450
my friend can't make it.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.260
It's too late to find a replacement.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:39.450
It'll be okay, Kirino.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.060
I have a plan.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.270
Really?

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.920
Yup. Leave it to me.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.870
Thank you, Panda.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:48.980
Thank you!

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.990
So that's the deal.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:55.700
I got the point.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:59.120
So you need members for 
the group blind date.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.820
So I'm thinking about asking Polar Bear.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.000
What do you think?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.410
What?! Not me?!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.750
Are you free today, Polar Bear?

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:11.710
Are you free today?

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.250
So it's not me.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.040
And I was listening so intently, too.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:24.550
But you kept saying that you 
were busy, Mr. Penguin.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:27.080
Well, yeah, but...

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.560
I think I could make

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.930
a few changes to go to 
the group blind date.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.780
You're busy, right?

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:39.080
Yeah, I guess I'm busy.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:41.240
You go have fun, then.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.240
Karaoke

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.620
Panda and Mr. Polar Bear? Why?

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.090
This would be the guys' team.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.930
Let's do our best, Mr. Handa.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.990
Sorry, Mr. Handa. Let's do our best.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.410
Well, let's go.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:15.960
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:15.960
To be continued in the second half.

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:14.230
To be continued in the second half.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:20.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:20.330
Mr. Handa's Group Blind Date!

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:26.200
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:26.330
Continuing from the first half.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.340
Continuing from the first half.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.620
Are you ready to order?

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.130
A polar bear?!

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:44.290
H-How about we start 
with introductions?

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:46.060
I'll start.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.140
My name is Kirino.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:52.020
I'm a zoo keeper. Nice to meet you.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:54.590
Now, your turn.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.340
I-I-I'm Handa.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.760
I-I humbly t-thank you

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:06.160
f-for i-inviting me to this 
f-formal group blind date today.

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:08.470
I am quite inexperienced in this venture,

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:11.160
but I'm pleased to make 
your acquaintance.

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.570
You're being too stiff.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.810
Your introduction doesn't 
have to be that formal.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.680
But this is the first 
time I'm meeting them.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.590
It's fine.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.840
Group blind dates aren't that formal.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:32.140
In addition, please allow me 
to introduce you to Panda,

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.690
who works with me.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.350
You're still being too stiff.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:38.690
I'm sorry, we brought a panda.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.990
I'm Panda!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.190
So cute!

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.450
<i>They don't seem to mind
 Panda being here.</i>

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.120
And then we have...

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:52.620
I'm Polar Bear. I run a café.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:54.600
Wow!

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:55.770
You run a café?

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:56.940
I want to go!

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.290
What's it called?

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:00.800
Polar Bear's Café.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.080
So straight to the point.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.180
By any chance, was it 
featured in any magazines?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.220
Every now and then.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.500
Wow! I've totally seen it before!

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.140
Is it okay if we stop by sometime?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.140
Of course.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:14.560
He's really popular, too.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:18.060
My hobbies include capturing seals.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.660
What's that?

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:22.070
Can you take us with you next time?

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.440
I don't think that's a good idea.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.490
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:28.580
Now it's our turn.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:29.660
I'm Hiromi!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.660
That's Hiromi.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.080
I'm Rika!

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:34.520
That's Rika.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.500
I'm Mizuki.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.190
That's Mizuki.

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.250
I know, I can hear them just fine.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.550
Go ahead with your order.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.470
Let's start off with draft beers.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:46.430
Got it.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.890
Let's start off with bamboo.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:49.900
Bamboo?

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.390
I'm sorry, we don't carry that...

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.310
Really? Then how about bamboo grass?

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.520
We don't have that either.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.730
Then what do you usually order?

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.430
We drink beer...

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.140
And eat edamame...

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.040
And fried chicken, too.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.950
Let's start off with seals.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.610
They don't have any.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:10.620
Can I bring some from home?

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:15.550
No. Let's just start with six 
draft beers and one juice.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:17.580
I want bamboo.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:21.540
I guess that makes sense, 
he is a panda after all.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.480
I totally want to see him eat it.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:25.260
That'd be so cute!

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.550
You should totally eat bamboo!

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.010
What kind of group blind date is this?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:37.710
I'm not saying that

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.650
I want to go to the group blind date.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.470
I see.

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:44.020
It's just I was the one listening

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.070
to Panda's story that whole time,

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:48.110
so wouldn't it be natural 
for him to ask me?

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:53.530
I have a penguin named Penko 
so I don't really want to go,

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.080
but perhaps to study social activities...

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:57.000
Did you want to go?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.070
I just told you that 
I didn't want to go.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:01.970
Come on, Miss Sasako.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:05.840
If he was going to invite someone,
he should've invited me instead of Polar Bear.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.960
That would be nice.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:09.930
Did you want to go?

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.530
Of course I did.

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:17.150
Argh! I bet everyone is having 
tons of fun right about now!

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.890
Could I get another café 
mocha, Miss Sasako?

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:20.930
Yes.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:25.470
So you're all friends from college?

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:26.860
Yup.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.820
Oh, do you have any 
capybaras at your zoo?

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.320
They're really popular right now.

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.490
Is a capybara really a rodent?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.960
Then is there a capybara 
hot spring at the zoo?

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:48.230
You should use your voice 
to answer, you know.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:51.590
Not to mention you haven't 
said a word for a while now.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:53.550
I should probably get going.

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:56.090
Do you have other plans?

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:59.070
I have to clean the bathroom.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.860
Whoa, Mr. Handa!

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:06.580
You totally can't say something 
like that in front of girls!

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:07.650
Is something wrong?

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:11.610
E-Everything is fine. 
Sorry, he's a little drunk.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.070
Did he say something 
about cleaning <i>(souji)</i>?

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:19.400
H-He said we should order 
some sausage <i>(so-se-ji)</i>!

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:20.640
Right?

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.790
I'll order some right now.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.260
Two sausage platters,

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.750
and a sashimi platter, too.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:29.640
Thanks, Polar Bear.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:32.750
Huh? Where's Panda?

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:37.180
Sorry about the wait!

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.120
We weren't waiting!

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:40.890
You actually went to get some?

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.850
Yeah, because they don't 
have anything here.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.690
What are you talking about?

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:48.210
See, like nuts and fried shrimp!

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:49.810
Thank you for the meal!

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.660
So cute!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.320
I've never seen a panda 
eat bamboo before!

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.200
Me, either!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.570
Me, either!

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:04.750
Can we take a picture?

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.220
Sure.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:10.430
It says right here you can't 
bring outside food or drink.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:11.920
If the server finds out...

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:14.320
Look over here!

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:14.880
Here you go...

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:15.820
Over here, over here!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:20.850
I'm sorry, I told him he 
can't bring that in here.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.150
So...

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:36.110
So cute! Can I take a picture, too?

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.040
Um... what about not 
bringing in outside...

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:41.130
Oh, it's totally fine!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:46.400
What animal do you take 
care of, Mr. Handa?

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.440
P-Pandas.

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:54.700
Pandas?! You take care of pandas?!

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:56.770
Y-Yes...

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.760
So cute!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.180
C-Cute?

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:06.140
Tell us more about the pandas!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.020
Polar 
Bear 
Café

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:10.260
Here he is sleeping.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:12.610
Wow, so cute!

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:14.810
This is him playing.

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:17.110
So cute!

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:19.540
Here he is lazing around.

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.950
Aww, so cute!

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:25.010
I'm surprised you can 
tell them all apart.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.050
Well, I am a professional.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.630
So cute!

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.170
Tell us more!

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:35.220
Pandas have short intestines

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.880
and can't get much 
nutrition from bamboo.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:43.230
That's why they're eating 
bamboo all day.

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:46.570
Wow, their intestines are short!

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:51.490
So cute!

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.160
Apparently that's cute, too.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:59.200
Tell them even more cute 
things about me, Mr. Handa.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:04.260
Since they only eat bamboo, 
pandas' poop smells good.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:07.020
It's similar to lemon.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.960
Oh, here we go.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.920
Yes, it smells like panda poop.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:12.860
Here, try it.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:20.110
Mr. Handa! I don't think they 
need that information.

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:23.800
Come on, tell them something 
cuter than that.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.350
Oh, really?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.370
Pandas look cute with their 
droopy eyes, right?

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:31.230
In actuality,

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:36.570
their actual eye is small and very sharp.

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:39.030
They don't need to know that either.

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:43.490
Really? I think that's really cute.

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:47.270
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.460
So cute!

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:53.130
Mr. Penguin,

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.090
here you go, your refill 
on the café mocha.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:59.800
Oh? He's not here.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:03.260
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:07.470
Is it okay if we come by the 
panda corner sometime?

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.980
Of course. Please come.

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:12.410
I'll introduce you to Mr. 
Full-time Panda, too.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.400
Mr. Full-time Panda?

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.460
So what's this panda, then?

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.380
He's a part-time panda that 
works two days a week.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.830
Oh, he's a part-timer.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:23.200
So cute!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.690
Is that cute?

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:27.100
It's totally cute.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.950
Right?

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:29.700
Oh!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.150
What's wrong?

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.580
Wh-What the?!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.710
A penguin?

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.220
Good evening.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.180
What brings you here?

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:48.140
Weren't you busy, Mr Penguin?

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.060
Well, um...

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:54.150
So cute!

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.520
Really?! That, too?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.520
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.350
<i>Ma-Ma-halo!</i>

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:00.440
Yay!

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:01.890
Yay!

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:03.200
Yay! Yay!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:04.160
Mr. Penguin,

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:05.820
could I have the mic now?

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.230
I'm singing one more song! 
One more song!

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.010
Oh, jeez...

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:13.460
Snoring?

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.370
He's asleep!

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:19.910
Wake up, Panda. Wake up!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.840
Mr. Handa, too?!

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.340
Look, they're asleep.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.800
Hey, don't they look alike?

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:33.920
<i>You lucky boys and girls 
who found this café</i>

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:34.730
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:39.830
Thank you very much for today.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.790
It was a lot of fun!

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:44.650
Tell us more about pandas next time!

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:48.120
Sure. Please visit the zoo.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:51.370
Sure! Well, good night.

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:58.270
Okay, I have to go clean my 
bathroom, so I'm heading off.

00:21:58.270 --> 00:21:59.550
See you tomorrow.

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:00.290
Okay.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:07.230
That's totally like Mr. Handa.

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:09.260
Did you want to have some 
coffee at my place?

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:12.220
Sure, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Ma-Ma-Ma-Ma-halo.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.000
Yay!

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.150
Huh?

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:20.890
Where'd everyone go?

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:24.860
The End

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:24.860
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:24.440
The End.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:25.390
Next Time

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.010
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:00.010 --> 00:24:01.290
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:04.880
How do you sit on the café 
chair, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:08.010
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:11.430
How do you sit on the café 
chair, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.090
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:15.260
How do you sit—

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:16.010
Let's end this!

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:19.540
Next time on Polar Bear 
Café, episode 80.

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:20.060
Enjoy.

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:21.500
Episode 11!

00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:24.480
Mr. Penguin's Broken Heart
Panda's Night Out

